    "label": {
      "en": "FYA- 2021- 2024"
    },
    "short_label": {
      "en": "$Minwage_hourly"
    },
    "description": {
      "en": "$Minwage_hourly is the hourly value of the French statutory minimum wage (SMIC horaire), latest modelled value €11.88, labelled by the modeller as covering the 2021-2024 period. It is one of the most heavily used constants in the France spine: it defines the dependent-child earnings threshold (DepChildCond) in TUDef_fr and bchlg_fr's tax-unit definitions and in bhotn_fr's tax-unit/BenCalc logic, matching the FR benefits note's rule that a child counts as dependent for family benefits (e.g. Allocation Familiale) only if their own earnings stay below a set share of SMIC computed over a fixed number of hours (the note cites '55% of SMIC (169 hours)'); it also sets the Comp_Cond compensation/eligibility condition in bch00_fr (extra benefit for families with 3+ children and an eldest child aged 20) and in bmact_fr/bpact_fr (eligibility based on a prior insurance/contribution record measured against the minimum wage); and it feeds the Formula in bsawk_fr's ArithOp function, which computes the individual earnings bonus within the Activity Allowance (Prime d'activité) - the FR note describes this bonus as applying progressively to earnings expressed relative to SMIC, up to one SMIC."
    },
    "explanation": {
      "en": "EUROMOD function group: Min Wage"
    },
